{
  "wire": "low-relay GET /presence — v1 of the THREE-STATE shape (#313 H1)",
  "why": [
    "Two components, two repos: the relay (rust-message-box handle_presence_route /",
    "presence_route_response) PRODUCES these bytes, and the LOW client",
    "(bsv-low app/src/lib/presence.ts fetchOpponentPresence / fetchLobbyHostPresence)",
    "CONSUMES them. Pinning each side against its own idea of the wire would pin",
    "two independent beliefs, not the agreement. So this file is the agreement:",
    "each repo drives its REAL code through every case here, and each repo's gate",
    "also asserts the sha256 of this file's bytes equals the constant recorded in",
    "the other repo's test. Edit one copy and BOTH gates go red until they match.",
    "",
    "The load-bearing case is `hub-fault`: a relay-internal failure (DO namespace,",
    "stub fetch, unreadable body) must NOT be spelled like an absence. It carries",
    "HTTP 503 and NO `present` key at all — the third state is unrepresentable as",
    "a boolean, not merely flagged beside one — and the client must read it as",
    "null/unknown. Before #313 that case was HTTP 200 `present:false`, and a 30s",
    "relay blip would have branded every probed live host 'away' at once.",
    "",
    "`presenceWire` is the producer SELF-IDENTIFYING: it appears only on a real",
    "answer (HTTP 200) and means 'this relay distinguishes a hub fault from an",
    "absence'. It exists because the fix ships as two independently-deployed",
    "components: until the relay carrying it is live, a client CANNOT tell an old",
    "build's fabricated `false` from a genuine one. Consumers that count `false`",
    "as EVIDENCE (the #309/#313 lobby away tag) therefore require the marker and",
    "read an unmarked `false` as unknown — see the `legacy-absence-no-marker`",
    "case. Consumers that only latch on `true` are unaffected either way."
  ],
